WEBVTT

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.050
I thought you would come, sooner or later.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:12.050
It's not like you to stay silent when you've had something precious taken from you.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.610
You're similar to my daughter in that regard, Teppei.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.580
That's something I've always thought about.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.690
The reason Mom fell in love with Dad.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.490
He resembled you quite a bit, Grandfather.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.620
Teppei, go ahead and unwrap the money.

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:43.280
This is...

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.440
One million yen.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.960
This is the first time I've seen this much at once, but it seems unexpectedly small.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:51.020
Small?

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:54.100
Small?  Indeed, it might seem that way, but in order to obtain it,

00:02:54.100 --> 00:03:02.350
a normal person would have to work several months, con someone, or steal it.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:06.280
I see.  You're right.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.710
Let me tell you about a certain man.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:12.280
He was able to get 600 million yen easily.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.920
What would you do if you had that money?

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.610
Start up a new company, or donate some of the money...

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:26.590
The man tried to increase his fortune to 1.2 billion yen, but he eventually fell into ruin.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:32.310
The more wealth you have, the more you lose sight of yourself.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:33.640
Do you understand?

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.050
I don't get it.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:38.830
It's fine if you don't understand right now.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:46.320
What you must not forget is to value your wealth as much as you value your own way of life.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:56.870
When using this sword, you must hold your beliefs as strong as the steel it's made of.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:01.450
Remember this.  Wealth is your sword.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:06.870
Your life will be built upon your wealth.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:12.210
Teppei, what shall you cut with the sword known as wealth?

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.120
Show me.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:21.600
All of those who work for the Arima Group will be depending on your single strike.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:31.880
Milord.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:37.760
Ah, what an uneasy expression.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.500
Does it bother you that Teppei is going to rescue Princess Charlotte?

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:47.230
Of course not!  I'm just a maid...

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.230
You're giving up of your own accord?

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:52.850
I-I...

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.860
I won't force you to say it.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:01.230
Ever since I took you in, I've tried to act like a father to you,

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:04.470
but I still don't know what to do in this kind of situation.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:09.820
This is the only thing I can think of.

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:15.950
Thank you, Milord.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:27.130
Yowsah!  A private jet?  I'd expect no less from you, Arima-sama!

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:32.190
It's not mine, though.  To be honest, it'll be my first time in an aircraft.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:38.600
Really?  Don't worry, it might be scary at first.  After you get used to it, it feels great!

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.600
H-Hey...

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.980
Geez, cut it out already!

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.730
Pig!  Pig!  You pig!

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:49.820
More!  More!  Step on me more!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:51.280
Ah, right there is good!

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:06.080
Hey, why are you staying silent?  It's not like you.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.600
What do you mean, it's not like me?

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:12.090
You usually let fly with the abusive language...

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:18.400
Abusive language?  Since when have I used that?!

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.270
Always.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.460
Well then, I'll use some abusive language right now.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:27.270
Going to rescue her even though she's already an ocean away is sheer idiocy!

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.990
Yea, that's more like it.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:32.030
You're kind of throwing off my rhythm here.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:39.480
You know...

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.930
I-If...

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:47.670
If I were to be kidnapped by someone, would you come and save me?

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.490
I-It's nothing!  Never mind!

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:56.770
I guess I do hate all of you Arimas after all.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.260
Don't come back!

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:01.090
Just go off somewhere!

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.930
Teppei...

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:17.910
I'm heading out, then.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.630
About your question...

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:35.860
I'd save you.  If you were kidnapped by someone,

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:38.330
I'd follow and use all my might to save you.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:44.970
Damn it...

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:51.370
He's pretty cool, damn it.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:01.570
This is Fujikura Yuu, under the direct supervision of Arima foundation heir Arima Teppei.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:07.600
Charlotte Hazelrink-sama is currently headed east on a unidentified train.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:10.670
The train is suspected to be the Grand Hazelrink.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:16.200
The Imperial train disappeared en route to its last scheduled destination,

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:20.680
and the person responsible is believed to be Hartman Vezelheim.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:26.180
The Grand Hazelrink is the train that links Hazelrink to the neighboring countries.

00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:27.680
I fear that if we act indiscreetly,

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:30.440
this may result in an international incident.

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:34.180
Similar to the prior incident at the Arima Hills,

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:37.450
thorough planning is required to resolve this situation most effectively.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:44.190
I would request the deployment of the Fil'mish Principality's cavalry by Sir Vincent van Hossen.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.410
I will gladly comply.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:52.440
Please help detail the layout of the train.  Kindly assist them, Alfred-sama.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:54.460
The one to rescue the Princess...

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:56.220
...shall be me!

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.040
<i>I'm bored!</i>

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.060
I'm bored, I'm bored, I'm <i>bored!</i>

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:07.970
W-Well then, shall we play Trump?

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:09.380
I'm tired of that!

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:10.840
How about Mah-jongg?

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.450
I don't understand the rules!

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:14.490
What about a card game?

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:15.750
I don't understand it!

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:17.590
T-Then, Niramekko?

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:17.590
Note: Niramekko is a game in which which two children staring at each other try to make their opponent laugh first.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:18.230
Eh?

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:21.320
There's no way I can win that!

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.070
Hartman-sama.

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:26.080
It appears the enemy has taken our bait.

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:27.580
Really?

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:28.690
Yes!

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:30.320
So it begins.

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.580
This is...

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:44.550
Yes, this is the Fil'mish Principality, Silvia-sama's home country.

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:47.580
Silvie.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:51.250
You're late, Teppei-dono.  I was beginning to have second thoughts.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:52.260
Sorry.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.810
Captain, preparations are complete.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:56.040
Understood.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:57.300
Captain?!

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:01.280
Through a series of events, I somehow became captain of my own cavalry unit.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.770
What do you mean, "through a series of events"?

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:06.370
She defeated the previous captain.

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:13.020
W-What the heck is with that?

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:16.540
I-It was nothing big, Teppei-dono, so I didn't tell you about it.

00:10:18.230 --> 00:10:19.180
Teppei-kun.

00:10:19.790 --> 00:10:22.170
Welcome to Fil'mish.

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:23.720
Vincent-san!

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:27.690
Although I wouldn't call it a welcoming ceremony, I've prepared a party.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:28.920
Enjoy yourself.

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:29.800
A party?

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.130
You will come as well, won't you?

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:35.090
I-I'm just a servant...

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:40.810
It's alright.  Tonight, we're setting aside rank and just getting along.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:56.880
It's odd to have a party when things are so serious.

00:10:57.410 --> 00:11:03.340
My father has always been like that.  Whenever things get too serious, he throws a party,

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:07.090
gathering people without a care for social standing.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:08.790
Is this okay?

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:12.160
It's fine!  Papa said so!

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:13.600
Well then...

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:18.020
It was ever since my mom died...

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:23.360
Though, he hasn't thrown a 'hot spring' party yet.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:25.990
Teppei-dono.

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:29.340
This is my mother.

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:31.530
She looks so beautiful.

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:34.050
Silvie, you look a lot like her.

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:36.730
Don't flatter me.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:38.380
It's not flattery.  I'm telling the truth.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:46.960
The first time I met you was at a party like this, wasn't it?

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.260
You're right.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.560
Swinging your sword around in the courtyard...

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.180
That's where you appeared.

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:55.570
How about it?  It's been a while, so how about a match?

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:56.800
Sounds great!

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:04.180
How's your home country?

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:06.580
Even though I have my childhood memories,

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:08.240
it still feels like I'm sightseeing.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:11.580
What kind of place were you born in?

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.990
You could see a narrow alleyway and the power lines.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:17.360
It was kind of a mess underneath the train tracks.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:19.060
Even so, I loved it.

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:21.570
I'm the same.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.580
This country has a lot of problems,

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:25.420
but I love it.

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:29.680
Silvie, I...

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.230
...have something I need to say.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:34.390
In coming here, you need to understand some things.

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:36.790
I work hard for this country,

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:38.430
and I fight for this country.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:40.580
You should do the same.

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:42.550
Japan is a great country,

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:44.020
but it's too kind for me!

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:54.110
It's my victory.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.480
I've lost completely.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.350
Let's pretend this duel didn't happen.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:04.680
I like strong men.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:08.120
I won't accept a man who has lost to me twice.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:26.210
Let's save Charl, Teppei-dono.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:27.630
All right.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:39.250
We have confirmed via satellite imagery that the train is indeed the Grand Hazelrink.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:42.710
If it continues to proceed, it will cross into Fil'mish.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.850
For a short period of time, correct?

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:49.100
We must rescue Charlotte-sama within that time frame!

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:58.690
Note: Ron is one means of winning a hand of Mahjong.

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:58.690
There!  Ron!

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:02.500
I win!  Tatechin, dora dora, baiman!

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:04.000
T-Tatechin?

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:04.900
B-Baiman?

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:09.550
W-Would you say that one more time?

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:12.400
Huh?  Don't tell me, I got it wrong?

00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:19.670
Note: Charlotte is saying some Mah-jongg terms that sound very similar to the Japanese words for "muddled" and "erection".

00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:19.670
T-Tatechin, dora dora, baiman?

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:23.790
After that, Ron!

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:28.170
Geez, that was quick.  You came right away.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:30.720
Yes, you were amazing!

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:31.980
I'm glad.

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:35.180
Heh, it's okay...

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:39.140
If we play together, we can understand each other, after all.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:42.450
I wasn't wrong.

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:43.350
Right?

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:47.340
Yep.

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:48.560
That's right!

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:04.970
The train has entered our country.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:05.750
Very well.

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:11.670
We are the van Hossen Cavalry Brigade of the Fil'mish Principality.

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:17.390
We have reason to believe that you are holding an important person aboard your train.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:19.190
Release her immediately.

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:20.950
Ignore her.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:24.280
This Grand Hazelrink will soon pass into another country.

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:27.960
This isn't something Fil'mish can handle.

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:29.390
<i>Advance!</i>

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.500
I repeat!  Release your hostage immediately!

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:37.240
If you fail to do so, we shall use force!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:40.210
That's right.  Get even angrier.

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:42.580
Hartman-sama.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:50.930
So you've come, Arima Teppei.

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:52.440
Speed it up.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:53.090
Yes.

00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:59.620
What's all the fuss?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:03.930
An unidentified motorbike is attempting to race the train, it seems.

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.350
I-I'll take this one!  Ah, just the card I needed---

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:08.350
Teppei!

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:13.570
Teppei!  Teppei came for me!

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:13.850
W-Wait!

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.030
He's getting closer!

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.520
They've fired on our soil!

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:26.530
Prepare to attack!

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:28.580
Cavalry unit, <i>charge!</i>

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.420
That's how it's got to be.

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:38.100
Teppei!

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:42.060
Milady!

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.260
You're not Teppei!

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:48.320
How dare you do this to Milady...

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:52.070
Alfred!

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:56.990
I, Alfred, will not forgive those who have laid hands on Milady!

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:10.580
It's impossible to infiltrate the train as it is.

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:15.790
However, if they are negligent and increase their speed, Teppei-sama should be able to infiltrate.

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:19.290
Alfred-sama, please create such an opportunity for Teppei-sama.

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:24.020
After they sustain the first damage, we will seize that opportunity.

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:36.480
Now!

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.350
So this is how it is...

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:43.180
Hartman-sama.

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:47.650
Arima Teppei from the front, cavalry from the rear...

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:51.330
Josephine.  Recover our captive.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.420
Yes!

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:54.840
The rest of you, deal with the cavalry.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:03.560
I'll never give up!

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:08.970
Alfred!

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:12.020
Capture her.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:13.240
Yes, ma'am!

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:24.240
Teppei!

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:26.130
Charl!

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:27.970
Don't make any sudden moves.

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:30.300
The Princess is valuable, after all.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:31.990
You bitch!

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.430
The train's speed is...

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:39.500
What's going on?  Don't tell me...they're undoing Teppei-dono's work?

00:18:43.540 --> 00:18:44.840
Teppei.

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:51.180
I'll make you disappear here.

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:53.320
Don't move.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:58.640
Hartman-sama appears to like that girl, but to me, honestly she's just in the way.

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:04.410
Rejoice!  At the very least, you get to die in the arms of the man you love.

00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:13.790
W-Why...?

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:20.780
Why...Hartman...?

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:22.780
You're a bother, Josephine.

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:25.260
You just couldn't follow the plan...

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:27.720
It's okay, though.

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:31.480
If you were still alive after this operation, it would be quite a scandal.

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:38.100
Hey!  Isn't she an ally of yours?!

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:43.660
When I was a boy, I used to visit the hotel in Hazelrink.

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:47.370
Of course, I wasn't spending the night.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:49.370
It was because I was poor.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:51.530
I was pickpocketing.

00:19:53.170 --> 00:20:00.010
Don't you think it would be better to beg for money, instead of using such underhanded means?

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:02.630
Committing such a foul deed,

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:05.920
have you no shame?

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:17.240
That man seemed like he had never been embarrassed in his whole life.

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:19.240
So, I swore that

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:21.030
even if it took my whole life,

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:26.010
I would make Arima Isshin suffer the same humiliation!

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:32.570
Alf-dono!

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:39.320
When I met with Arima Isshin not too long ago, I had an inspiration.

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:46.250
Acting as I once had, the Hazelrink-Fil'mish Resort plan began.

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:49.750
The rest of the train is just getting in the way.

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:56.090
Milady!

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:56.090
Teppei-dono!

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:02.020
Charlotte and her beloved, the heir to the Arima Foundation.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:09.030
I shall take everything from Arima Isshin, and advance my own plan that much closer to fruition.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:12.110
You've only helped me in that regard,

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:13.960
Arima Teppei!

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:22.000
Charl!

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:31.600
Charl.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:32.600
Teppei!

